# decision Pub uses the native nested Git descriptor

The Pub adapter owns one two-space-indented entry under top-level `dependencies`. It writes
`git.url`, `git.ref`, and optional `git.path`; locked refs are the full lock commit and floating
refs are the declared branch. It splices only that YAML entry, preserving every unrelated byte.
Inline dependency maps are rejected as not wirable instead of being reformatted.
If top-level `dependencies` is absent, the adapter creates a delimited mapping and removes the
container as a unit on unwire.

# decision pubspec.lock stays downstream

Wiring does not run `dart pub get`: resolution may update unrelated packages. Consumers refresh
`pubspec.lock` in their normal Dart or Flutter workflow.

# test Pub adapter

- Fixture/golden wiring is idempotent and preserves comments and unrelated dependencies.
- A subdirectory export writes `git.path`; drift checks URL and locked ref.
- Unwire restores the original fixture bytes.
